# Moth Template title

-- this is Markdown body text, not a Moth comment.

Backslashes such as \ remain body text, while `inline code` uses paired backticks.

[p:
    This paragraph is parsed as a nested Moth template inside the implicit `$md` body.

    - This nested body should use Markdown list highlighting.

    [child:
        * This deeper template should also use Markdown.

        # Heading to make it obvious
    ]
]

[
    section,
    $md:
    ## Multiline template head

    This remains Markdown.
]

[raw_content, $raw:
    - This explicit formatter should not use Markdown list highlighting.
]

[escaped_content, $escape_html:
    <strong>This is escaped content.</strong>
]

[$doc:
    ## Documentation comment

    This should highlight like `$md`, including `inline code`.

    [codeblock, $code("moth"):
        @docs/pages/home render as render_home
        @docs/pages/about content as about_content
    ]
]

[$todo:
    This should look like ordinary Moth comment text.
    It should still have a distinct todo template scope.
]

[$note:
    This should also look like ordinary Moth comment text.
    It should still have a distinct note template scope.
]

Literal delimiters use string insertion: ["[literal]"]

@https://example.com (link)
